      ":question/problem": "Which of the following diagrams gives the slope field at the points indicated for the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-1-(2)xy?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We have to sketch the slope field at the points $(-1,-1)$,$(-3,3)$,$(-2,0)$.\n\nTo sketch the slope field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the right-hand side of the differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-1,-1)}=-1-2(-1)(-1)=-3, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-3,3)}=-1-2(-3)(3)=17, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-2,0)}=-1-2(-2)(0)=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting up our points and drawing our line segments, we get the following diagram.\n\n![](images/03/03868ccfb13e15fa6a92adb2a856d6e40537d2e7a23584a31ef292ce3ebd410c.png)",
